        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 rounded-2xl p-8 text-gray-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="mb-4">
            Grey but sound: seal it. Ravelling, spider cracks and shallow dips on a firm base: skim it with a trowel-grade resurfacer, then seal it. Alligatoring, heaving, potholes or anything that moves underfoot: the base has failed and it needs cutting out and rebuilding, then an overlay or a replacement.
          </p>
          <p class="m-0">
            Repair, resurface, seal, in that order and with a proper cure between each. And do not let a pail that says "restores" talk you into a coating when the driveway is telling you it needs a base.
          </p>
